---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GlassCard from '../components/GlassCard.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'May 16, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Cookies and trackers | BabyBlocks"
  description="What babyblocks.io stores in your browser, what it tracks, and what it does not. No cookies, no third-party ad pixels."
  canonical="/cookies"
>
  <section class="sec-hero section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-hero-inner">
        <div class="label-chip">Cookies</div>
        <h1>This website doesn't use cookies.<br /><span class="text-gradient">Here's the full picture anyway.</span></h1>
        <p>
          We could have written a 3,000-word cookie policy. Instead, the honest version is short:
          babyblocks.io sets no cookies, uses one privacy-friendly analytics tool, and loads no
          third-party ad pixels. The detail is below.
        </p>
        <p class="sec-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard accent padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="check" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>The short version</h2>
            <ul class="sec-list">
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Zero cookies set by babyblocks.io itself.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Zero advertising or social-media tracking pixels.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> One first-party, cookieless analytics tool (Plausible) to count page views and form submissions.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> A small amount of <code>localStorage</code> is used for UI preferences only (such as remembering whether you dismissed a banner).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="bar-chart-2" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Analytics</h2>
            <p>
              We use <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible Analytics</a>
              to understand which pages are visited, which forms are submitted, and which links are clicked.
              Plausible is <strong>cookieless by design</strong>. It does not use cookies,
              does not collect personal data, does not build a profile of you, and does not share data
              with anyone else. Page-view data is aggregated and anonymized at the source.
            </p>
            <p>
              What Plausible records when you visit: the URL you opened, the page that linked to you (if any),
              your browser, your operating system, and your country. It does not record your IP address,
              your screen size, your name, your email, or anything you type into the page.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you want to block analytics anyway, the standard browser-level Do Not Track and
              tracker-blocking extensions (uBlock Origin, Brave Shields, Firefox Enhanced Tracking Protection)
              already block Plausible without us needing to do anything.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="info" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Local storage</h2>
            <p>
              A small amount of data is kept in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> for UI state only.
              Typical examples: remembering that you closed a one-time announcement banner, or your
              choice of theme if you override the system preference. None of this is sent to our servers,
              and clearing your browser data wipes it instantly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="x-circle" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>What we do not do</h2>
            <ul class="sec-list muted">
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> No Google Analytics, no Google Tag Manager.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> No Facebook Pixel, no Meta tracking, no TikTok Pixel, no LinkedIn Insight Tag.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> No advertising cookies. We do not run advertising.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> No cross-site tracking. We do not build a profile of you across the web.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> No session replay. We do not record your scrolling, clicking, or typing.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> No data shared or sold to anyone.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="smartphone" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>iOS apps</h2>
            <p>
              The BudgetBaby and PantryBaby apps do not run in a browser, so cookies do not apply.
              For the in-app analytics, crash reporting, and subscription handling that the apps use,
              see the per-product privacy policies:
              <a href="/budgetbaby/privacy">BudgetBaby Privacy</a> and
              <a href="/pantrybaby/privacy">PantryBaby Privacy</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="mail" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Questions</h2>
            <p>
              Email <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a> if you spot a
              tracker on this site that we have not disclosed. We will either explain it or remove it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .sec-hero { padding-top: calc(var(--space-20) + var(--space-8)); }
  .sec-hero-inner { max-width: 720px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .sec-hero-inner h1 { font-size: clamp(var(--text-4xl), 6vw, var(--text-6xl)); letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .sec-hero-inner p { font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 56ch; }
  .sec-updated { font-size: var(--text-xs) !important; color: var(--text-muted) !important; max-width: none !important; }
  .sec-section { padding-block: var(--space-4); }
  .sec-block { display: flex; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .sec-block-icon { color: var(--accent-light); flex-shrink: 0; padding-top: var(--space-1); }
  .sec-block h2 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .sec-block p { font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .sec-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .sec-block code { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .sec-block a { color: var(--accent-light); text-decoration: none; }
  .sec-block a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .sec-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; }
  .sec-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-2); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .sec-list.muted li { color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
